# Native amd64 build — HARDENED — for the hugmesh-host k8s/GPU worker.
#
# Variables substituted at build time:
#   @@CHOST@@       Host triplet (x86_64-pc-linux-gnu)
#   @@JOBS@@        Parallel make jobs
#   @@WORK_DIR@@    Base build directory

CHOST="@@CHOST@@"

# Generic, portable hardened flags. -march=native would tie the image to the
# build host's CPU; x86-64-v2 is a safe baseline for modern desktops/servers.
# NOTE: do NOT add -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE here — the hardened profile/toolchain already
# defines it, and a second definition on the command line makes packages that set
# their own (e.g. sys-apps/policycoreutils, which builds -Werror) fail with
# "_FORTIFY_SOURCE redefined [-Werror]". FORTIFY is retained via the hardened default.
# -Wno-error=... downgrades GCC-15's now-default *errors* (implicit-function-
# declaration etc.) back to warnings so older C (e.g. grub's makedev in getroot.c)
# still builds; KSPP/SSP/relro hardening is unaffected.
COMMON_FLAGS="-march=x86-64-v2 -O2 -pipe -fstack-protector-strong -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration -Wno-error=incompatible-pointer-types -Wno-error=int-conversion -Wno-error=implicit-int"
CFLAGS="${COMMON_FLAGS}"
CXXFLAGS="${COMMON_FLAGS}"
LDFLAGS="-Wl,-O1 -Wl,--as-needed -Wl,-z,relro -Wl,-z,now"

# -l@@JOBS@@ lets the parallel C builds self-throttle on shared load average.
# This is the SOLE global MAKEOPTS source (the chroot heredoc no longer exports
# one) so that per-package package.env caps (env/llvm-lowmem.conf -> llvm/clang
# at -j4) actually override it; an exported MAKEOPTS would shadow package.env.
MAKEOPTS="-j@@JOBS@@ -l@@JOBS@@"
# -userfetch/-userpriv: don't drop to the 'portage' user (can't traverse a
# mode-700 / encrypted work dir). Sandbox off for the native chroot build.
FEATURES="buildpkg nostrip -userfetch -userpriv -usersandbox -sandbox -pid-sandbox -network-sandbox -ipc-sandbox"
# Chroot-INTERNAL cache paths. The old @@WORK_DIR@@/{pkgdir,distfiles} rendered
# to the HOST-absolute build dir, which inside the chroot resolves UNDER the
# sysroot (sysroot/home/...): binpkgs+distfiles (2.4 GB) then got baked into
# every stage4/.img/squashfs (var/cache IS excluded; that home path was not),
# leaking host paths and bloating artifacts. /var/cache is excluded from the
# stage4 tar + squashfs, so these never ship, and they persist across the 4
# roles in one shared sysroot so role 2-4 reuse role 1's binpkgs (--usepkg).
PKGDIR="/var/cache/binpkgs"
DISTDIR="/var/cache/distfiles"
# ── Distfile fetch BOUND (issue #322) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Portage's default fetcher is `wget -t 3 -T 60`. -T is a READ timeout: it fires
# only when NO byte arrives for 60 s. A transfer that stalls but still trickles
# never trips it. Measured 2026-09-08 on the standalone-thick payload:
# media-fonts/noto's 1.02 GB GitHub archive stopped at 10.3 % and moved 0 bytes in
# 22 minutes while the fetcher sat at 0.5 % CPU, and the whole payload blocked for
# over an hour behind it — no gate, no WARN, a log that stopped mid-line. wget has
# no minimum-rate option at all (re-measured on the build host on 2026-09-16:
# `wget -T 10 --read-timeout=10` against a 1-byte-per-2-s trickle ran until it was
# killed from outside). curl has one: --speed-limit B --speed-time S aborts when
# the transfer averages under B bytes/s for S seconds, measured to fire in exactly
# S seconds against the same trickle. So the x86 fetch is curl, bounded to
# >= 10 KiB/s over any 60 s window, with curl's own retries (every attempt bounded
# the same way) before portage moves to the next mirror: worst case ~5 minutes per
# URI, not an hour. curl ships in the stage3 seed (verified in the 20260830
# hardened tarball), so this holds from the first chroot emerge, and the build
# never depcleans it out, so it holds on the device too.
#
# RESUMECOMMAND cannot be a plain `curl -C -`: GitHub's archive endpoint answers a
# Range request with 200 (no Content-Range), and curl then exits 33 "server does
# not seem to support byte ranges" WITHOUT downloading — the partial would never
# complete. The wrapper resumes when the server can, and on exit 33 falls back to a
# fresh bounded fetch of the whole file (the only thing that works against such a
# host; wget -c did the same, silently). Escaping follows make.globals'
# FETCHCOMMAND_SSH: \" and \$ survive portage's make.conf parse as " and $ for the
# outer command; \\\" and \\\$ survive BOTH the parse and the fetch-time expansion
# as literal quotes and dollars inside the bash -c script. EXECUTED, not read:
# tests/scripts/test-x86-fetchcommand-bound.sh renders this file the way the
# builder does and runs both commands against local healthy / trickling / silent /
# 404 / Range-ignoring / Range-capable servers.
FETCHCOMMAND="curl -f -L -g -sS --connect-timeout 30 --speed-limit 10240 --speed-time 60 --retry 3 --retry-delay 15 --max-redirs 5 -A \"Portage (Gentoo, https://www.gentoo.org) distfile-fetch\" -o \"\${DISTDIR}/\${FILE}\" \"\${URI}\""
RESUMECOMMAND="bash -c \"curl -f -L -g -sS --connect-timeout 30 --speed-limit 10240 --speed-time 60 --retry 3 --retry-delay 15 --max-redirs 5 -A \\\"Portage (Gentoo, https://www.gentoo.org) distfile-fetch\\\" -C - -o \\\"\\\$1\\\" \\\"\\\$2\\\"; rc=\\\$?; [ \\\"\\\$rc\\\" -eq 33 ] || exit \\\"\\\$rc\\\"; exec curl -f -L -g -sS --connect-timeout 30 --speed-limit 10240 --speed-time 60 --retry 3 --retry-delay 15 --max-redirs 5 -A \\\"Portage (Gentoo, https://www.gentoo.org) distfile-fetch\\\" -o \\\"\\\$1\\\" \\\"\\\$2\\\"\" hugmesh-resume \"\${DISTDIR}/\${FILE}\" \"\${URI}\""
# Persist per-package build logs (default temp build.log is wiped on clean, so a
# compile failure's cause is lost). Keeps every package's log under this dir for
# post-mortem of OOM/compile failures. Excluded from artifacts (it's under /var/log
# which the stage4 keeps, but it's small text; harmless).
PORTAGE_LOGDIR="/var/log/portage/build"

# Hardened USE baseline + container runtime + (optional) vendor-agnostic GPU stack.
# @@GPU_USE@@ expands to the GPU USE flags (vulkan vaapi vdpau gbm egl gles2) for
# the be+gpu / omnibus roles, and to nothing for the headless pki/be/fe roles.
USE="bindist hardened pie ssp -X -gtk -qt5 -qt6 -systemd -pulseaudio -bluetooth"
USE="${USE} cgroup cgroup2 seccomp selinux containers netlink"
USE="${USE} @@GPU_USE@@"
# @@CLIENT_USE@@ expands to the desktop USE (X gtk dbus elogind udev [+pulseaudio
# pipewire for --desktop full]) for the CLIENT roles (laptop/chromebook/desktop),
# and to nothing for node roles. It is appended LAST so it OVERRIDES the hardened
# headless -X/-gtk posture above on client builds only.
USE="${USE} @@CLIENT_USE@@"

# Build only the MCS SELinux policy: provision_selinux() and containerd's per-pod
# MCS labelling both target type=mcs. Pinning this avoids relying on the profile
# default and skips compiling the unused strict/targeted/mls stores (faster build).
POLICY_TYPES="mcs"

# Open, vendor-agnostic GPU: AMD (amdgpu/radeonsi), Intel (i915/iris),
# NVIDIA via nouveau. No proprietary blobs. @@VIDEO_CARDS@@ expands to that list
# for the be+gpu / omnibus roles, and to nothing (no DRI drivers) for headless
# pki/be/fe roles.
VIDEO_CARDS="@@VIDEO_CARDS@@"
# Xorg input drivers: "libinput" for client desktop roles (keyboard/mouse/touchpad),
# empty for headless nodes. Materialized by x11-base/xorg-drivers (packages-desktop).
INPUT_DEVICES="@@INPUT_DEVICES@@"

ACCEPT_LICENSE="* -@EULA"
ACCEPT_KEYWORDS="amd64"

GRUB_PLATFORMS="efi-64 pc"

# PYTHON_TARGETS / PYTHON_SINGLE_TARGET are DELIBERATELY NOT SET HERE.
# They are DERIVED FROM THE STAGE3 SEED at build time and appended to the
# rendered make.conf by scripts/_python-targets-lib.sh (pt_apply_seed_targets).
# A frozen python3_NN literal in this file is a BUG: the seed's python floats per
# arch and per snapshot (amd64 20260726 ships 3.13+3.14 and no 3.12; arm64 ships
# 3.14 only; the 2026-07 jetson seed shipped 3.12+3.14), and a USE_EXPAND
# assignment here REPLACES the profile default rather than widening it — which is
# what wedged the 2026-07-29 mesh build in a dev-python slot conflict, and, in
# mirror image, what produced the 2026-07-16 jetson "USE changes are necessary:
# python_targets_python3_12" wall. See docs/PYTHON-TARGETS-SEED-DRIFT.md.

# Server nodes have no interactive users; skip documentation and man pages.
# Client roles keep man pages (desktop users) but still drop doc/info.
# @@INSTALL_MASK@@ is substituted by the builder based on ROLE_CLIENT.
INSTALL_MASK="@@INSTALL_MASK@@"

PAX_MARKINGS="none"
